      "content": "Example: Finite Recursion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In this example, we will create a program to find the sum of natural numbers using recursion."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "# sum of natural numbers n\ntotal = 1 + 2 + ... + n"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Source Code"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1def calculate_sum(n):\n2\n3    if n != 0:\n4       # recursive call\n5        n = n + calculate_sum(n-1)\n6    \n7    return n\n8    \n9\n10result = calculate_sum(3)\n11print(result)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the recursive function call is made only when n is not equal to 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To meet this condition, we have decreased the value of n by 1 in each function call using calculate_sum(n-1). When n becomes 0, the recursive calls end."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Next, we'll see how this program works with visual illustration."
